  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norway&apos;s contribution to the Crisis Response Plan for Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the beginning of 2022, Somalia has been struck by an interlinked cluster of crises and conflict. While still recovering by one of the most severe droughts in the last decades that has driven mass displacement, widespread death of livestock and a devastating food and water crisis, the country is currently being impacted with heavy rains brought by El Ni&#xf1;o weather phenomena, which is causing extreme flooding, leading to destruction of infrastructure, crops, and human losses. 
 
With the main objectives of reducing threats and vulnerabilities through humanitarian protection, and widening the access for migrants, displaced persons and communities live to essential services and contribute to sustainable development, IOM proposes an integrated intervention to strengthen community-based protection structures and building the capacity of humanitarian actors. These efforts strive towards the overall objective of reducing exposure to protection risks, and/or harm experienced in the communities.</narrative>
  </description>
